1
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:09,520
‎I'm goin' home early! Hey, hey, hey, hey!

2
00:00:10,770 --> 00:00:12,940
‎SEASONAL SPRING VEG SALE
‎GREAT VALUE - PICKED TODAY

3
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:15,940
‎Next, please.

4
00:00:17,480 --> 00:00:18,480
‎Okay.

5
00:00:19,030 --> 00:00:20,200
‎20% OFF - HALF PRICE
‎ALCOHOL - RICE CRACKERS

6
00:00:30,580 --> 00:00:32,290
‎That'll be 1, 040 yen.

7
00:00:32,369 --> 00:00:33,710
‎Okay.

8
00:00:33,790 --> 00:00:36,080
‎Here is your change.

9
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:40,340
‎-You should have enough points soon.
‎-Okay.

10
00:00:40,420 --> 00:00:43,340
‎You'll get a coupon
‎for 50% off rice crackers tomorrow.

11
00:00:44,050 --> 00:00:45,220
‎Thanks.

12
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:56,320
‎Yamada. Time to swap out.

13
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:58,360
‎Something's up.

14
00:00:58,440 --> 00:00:59,440
‎TYPICALLY

15
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:01,110
‎Wow, so many points!

16
00:01:01,190 --> 00:01:02,610
‎Thank you very much.

17
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:06,620
‎My customer service
‎fell short of raising spirits.

18
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:07,700
‎Did it?

19
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:15,500
‎I need a cigarette.

20
00:01:16,170 --> 00:01:18,170
‎I hope I'll see you again, Sasaki.

21
00:02:58,940 --> 00:03:00,980
‎Tayama--

22
00:03:04,190 --> 00:03:07,440
‎I probably shouldn't smoke here
‎just 'cause it'll be easy for me to do so.

23
00:03:08,740 --> 00:03:11,030
‎Hello. I'm an easy woman.

24
00:03:13,620 --> 00:03:14,950
‎Tayama?

25
00:03:15,450 --> 00:03:16,990
‎'Sup?

26
00:03:18,580 --> 00:03:20,870
‎-Did you just finish your shift?
‎-Yep.

27
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:22,590
‎Good work today.

28
00:03:22,670 --> 00:03:24,630
‎More to the point, 
‎you came for a smoke, right?

29
00:03:24,710 --> 00:03:25,960
‎You came for me, right?

30
00:03:26,050 --> 00:03:27,470
‎Come on in.

31
00:03:27,550 --> 00:03:29,640
‎Okay. Please excuse my intrusion.

32
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:39,770
‎That's an awfully big sigh.

33
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:42,780
‎Had a bad day, Sasaki?

34
00:03:42,850 --> 00:03:45,690
‎Well, I guess so.

35
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:52,410
‎Yamada's worried about you.

36
00:03:53,660 --> 00:03:56,540
‎I wonder, was I unpleasant toward her?

37
00:03:56,620 --> 00:03:57,660
‎You weren't.

38
00:03:58,450 --> 00:04:01,660
‎She just thought you seemed down, and
‎she's worried about whether you're okay.

39
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:09,510
‎That Yamada really is
‎a wonderful and attentive store clerk.

40
00:04:10,010 --> 00:04:12,010
‎And thank you too, Tayama.

41
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:14,220
‎I'm just the messenger.

42
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:18,810
‎But didn't you go out of your way
‎to come and tell me this?

43
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:22,390
‎And your hair is down.

44
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:26,030
‎Maybe you couldn't wait
‎to get here and tell me--

45
00:04:27,270 --> 00:04:28,850
‎Tayama!

46
00:04:28,940 --> 00:04:31,400
‎You shouldn't blow smoke
‎in people's faces!

47
00:04:36,410 --> 00:04:39,200
‎My hair's this way
‎because I was feeling lazy.

48
00:04:40,410 --> 00:04:42,250
‎And as for why I wanted to tell you...

49
00:04:45,330 --> 00:04:47,000
‎I'm not gonna say.

50
00:04:47,590 --> 00:04:50,510
‎Because you're being cheeky today.

51
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:55,010
‎Cheeky? What?

52
00:04:55,550 --> 00:04:57,550
‎How am I being cheeky?

53
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:59,480
‎You're very cheeky for someone so dense.

54
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:01,730
‎No! I'm not dense!

55
00:05:07,110 --> 00:05:09,360
‎Maybe I am dense.

56
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:10,480
‎What happened?

57
00:05:11,230 --> 00:05:13,320
‎Well, Tayama...

58
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:18,320
‎I'd appreciate
‎your objective feedback here.

59
00:05:18,410 --> 00:05:19,410
‎Shoot.

60
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:22,910
‎Am I actually scary?

61
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:26,540
‎Are you all right?

62
00:05:26,620 --> 00:05:29,120
‎Why are you asking
‎such a strange question?

63
00:05:29,210 --> 00:05:30,500
‎Is it strange?

64
00:05:31,090 --> 00:05:32,180
‎Well, you see...

65
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:40,520
‎I made the new grad cry today.

66
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:44,350
‎Wait, what? Are you the type
‎to fly off the handle at work?

67
00:05:44,430 --> 00:05:45,600
‎That is so funny.

68
00:05:45,690 --> 00:05:48,110
‎Why, you... Why, you!

69
00:05:48,190 --> 00:05:49,900
‎No! I do not!

70
00:05:50,940 --> 00:05:53,030
‎It was such a minor mistake, 

71
00:05:53,110 --> 00:05:55,400
‎so I was trying to cheer her up.

72
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:58,440
‎But I must have come across
‎as the complete opposite.

73
00:06:02,370 --> 00:06:03,790
‎KEEP THINGS TIDY AND IN ORDER

74
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:06,090
‎Better luck next time.

75
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:10,300
‎Wait.

76
00:06:12,380 --> 00:06:14,670
‎What the hell did you do, Sasaki?

77
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:16,300
‎I'm very sorry.

78
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:19,550
‎Poor Sasaki really got chewed out, hey?

79
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:21,350
‎I hear he made the new grad cry.

80
00:06:21,430 --> 00:06:23,560
‎What? Our Sasaki?

81
00:06:26,770 --> 00:06:30,650
‎I'd hate to think she hates
‎her job now because of me.

82
00:06:37,530 --> 00:06:39,320
‎So what if she does?

83
00:06:39,410 --> 00:06:42,040
‎Your job involves
‎tolerating a shitty toxic workplace

84
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:44,620
‎that makes you work
‎late into the night, right?

85
00:06:44,700 --> 00:06:46,080
‎She's gonna leave no matter what.

86
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:48,290
‎Oh, Tayama.

87
00:06:50,830 --> 00:06:54,830
‎And if she's a new grad, that means
‎she's only just joined the company, yeah?

88
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:58,340
‎She'll figure it out soon enough.

89
00:06:58,420 --> 00:07:00,670
‎She'll know that you're a good egg.

90
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:07,650
‎Well, that is if she doesn't quit first.

91
00:07:08,310 --> 00:07:09,600
‎Thank you.

92
00:07:14,320 --> 00:07:18,070
‎I'll bet this sort of thing
‎never happens to Yamada.

93
00:07:18,780 --> 00:07:20,320
‎Why Yamada, of all people?

94
00:07:20,410 --> 00:07:24,620
‎Well, I was just thinking
‎I'll bet Yamada wouldn't scare a new grad, 

95
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:27,120
‎nor would she make them cry.

96
00:07:28,710 --> 00:07:33,210
‎You mean unlike me, who must
‎scare people off based off looks alone.

97
00:07:33,710 --> 00:07:35,800
‎No, I didn't mean it like that.

98
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:39,130
‎True, Yamada may be the type
‎who gets looked down upon, 

99
00:07:39,220 --> 00:07:41,810
‎but she's definitely not the scary type.

100
00:07:41,890 --> 00:07:43,980
‎Looked down upon?

101
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:48,220
‎I think she's amazing.

102
00:07:48,730 --> 00:07:51,150
‎She works late into the night, 
‎and she does it with a smile, 

103
00:07:51,230 --> 00:07:53,980
‎and she even worries herself
‎over customers like me.

104
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:58,020
‎I wish I could plug away with a smile
‎the way Yamada does.

105
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:07,410
‎It's 'cause the supermarket
‎is always making us practice our smiles.

106
00:08:07,490 --> 00:08:08,910
‎Really?

107
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,960
‎Even you?

108
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:12,040
‎Yeah.

109
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:15,790
‎"Squint to make little crescent-moon eyes.
‎Flex your facial muscles.

110
00:08:16,380 --> 00:08:18,170
‎Show your upper teeth."

111
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:21,680
‎Like this!

112
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:27,510
‎Tayama... You...

113
00:08:35,270 --> 00:08:37,190
‎Sorry. I'm so sorry.

114
00:08:38,150 --> 00:08:40,950
‎I mean, you kind of scared me there.

115
00:08:41,740 --> 00:08:45,120
‎What a lovely, 
‎sweet smile you have, Tayama.

116
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:51,710
‎Tayama?

117
00:08:53,540 --> 00:08:56,500
‎Now it's my turn to say sorry, Sasaki.

118
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:59,460
‎You see, it's faster to do it this way
‎than with just a demonstration.

119
00:08:59,550 --> 00:09:02,720
‎Sorry, Tayama. Are you mad?

120
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:06,470
‎I really didn't mean it.

121
00:09:08,300 --> 00:09:11,180
‎All right. Smile Practice is over.

122
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:20,150
‎Sorry, Tayama.

123
00:09:21,730 --> 00:09:24,230
‎Remember what I taught you, 
‎and make me proud.

124
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:25,820
‎-But I--
‎-Got it?

125
00:09:25,910 --> 00:09:26,910
‎Yes, ma'am!

126
00:09:27,950 --> 00:09:30,080
‎HAPPY CORP.

127
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:33,870
‎I am very sorry about yesterday.

128
00:09:35,420 --> 00:09:38,630
‎I didn't mean to start crying, but...

129
00:09:38,710 --> 00:09:41,670
‎But it all just sort of came out.

130
00:09:41,750 --> 00:09:43,710
‎It's smoky in here, 
‎so let's take this outside.

131
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:45,220
‎No, it's fine.

132
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:49,770
‎I'm very sorry
‎for making you out to be the bad guy.

133
00:09:49,850 --> 00:09:52,770
‎No, I should have been
‎more careful with my words.

134
00:09:52,850 --> 00:09:54,350
‎That's not true at all.

135
00:09:54,430 --> 00:09:58,560
‎I know you're a good person, and still I...

136
00:09:58,650 --> 00:09:59,650
‎What?

137
00:10:00,610 --> 00:10:02,900
‎She'll figure it out soon enough.

138
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:05,770
‎She'll know that you're a good egg.

139
00:10:09,660 --> 00:10:12,580
‎Everyone makes mistakes
‎when they're first starting out.

140
00:10:12,660 --> 00:10:14,450
‎Try not to let it get to you.

141
00:10:14,540 --> 00:10:17,340
‎If you ever need any help, 
‎please feel free to reach out.

142
00:10:17,830 --> 00:10:19,120
‎Thank you.

143
00:10:19,630 --> 00:10:21,630
‎LET'S KEEP THIS PLACE
‎NEAT AND TIDY

144
00:10:22,210 --> 00:10:23,460
‎You sweet talker, you.

145
00:10:23,550 --> 00:10:26,050
‎Stop that! Don't ruin it!

146
00:10:26,130 --> 00:10:28,550
‎SUPER S

147
00:10:31,010 --> 00:10:33,800
‎Next, please.

148
00:10:38,230 --> 00:10:40,320
‎Here is your receipt.

149
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:42,820
‎Thank you.

150
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:44,940
‎Thank you, and have a nice day.

151
00:10:56,660 --> 00:11:01,000
‎What a lovely, 
‎sweet smile you have, Tayama.

152
00:11:02,210 --> 00:11:04,000
‎How dare you laugh, Sasaki?

153
00:11:07,010 --> 00:11:09,050
‎You should be used to it.

154
00:11:25,110 --> 00:11:28,740
‎I came out for smokes with only
‎one layer on because it's spring.

155
00:11:28,820 --> 00:11:31,030
‎But it still gets quite cold out at night.

156
00:11:32,740 --> 00:11:35,200
‎Maybe I'll just have one puff
‎before heading home.

157
00:11:38,330 --> 00:11:41,580
‎Yamada. Time to swap out.

158
00:11:41,670 --> 00:11:42,800
‎'Kay.

159
00:11:48,050 --> 00:11:50,470
‎He didn't stop by today.

160
00:11:50,550 --> 00:11:53,260
‎Is he working overtime?
‎Staying the night? Until morning?

161
00:11:53,760 --> 00:11:55,970
‎Oh, and Yamada...

162
00:11:56,060 --> 00:11:57,310
‎Yes?

163
00:11:57,390 --> 00:12:00,980
‎The store manager wants
‎to speak with you before you leave.

164
00:12:09,150 --> 00:12:10,230
‎Tayama. Good eve--

165
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:13,120
‎MOODY

166
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:14,200
‎Oh, my.

167
00:12:14,280 --> 00:12:15,610
‎SOMEBODY'S CRANKY...

168
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:23,370
‎Well, if it isn't good old Sasaki.

169
00:12:23,460 --> 00:12:24,460
‎Hello.

170
00:12:24,540 --> 00:12:26,920
‎Well, don't just stand there.
‎Come sit with me.

171
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,170
‎Right.

172
00:12:33,470 --> 00:12:37,390
‎-Is everything all right--
‎-Sasaki. Did you have today off?

173
00:12:38,430 --> 00:12:40,060
‎Yes, strangely enough.

174
00:12:41,850 --> 00:12:44,140
‎Just what you'd say
‎when you have a toxic workplace.

175
00:12:51,490 --> 00:12:53,200
‎I'm glad you got the day off.

176
00:13:09,380 --> 00:13:12,300
‎COLD - WARM

177
00:13:12,380 --> 00:13:13,920
‎Not smoking today?

178
00:13:14,010 --> 00:13:16,300
‎It's cold out, so I need a drink.

179
00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:18,300
‎Would you like one too?

180
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:23,270
‎If you're feeling a little off, 

181
00:13:23,350 --> 00:13:28,310
‎don't they always say a warm drink
‎is better than smokes or alcohol?

182
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:37,320
‎I got a complaint.
‎First one in a long time.

183
00:13:37,410 --> 00:13:40,160
‎"She's always got great customer service, 

184
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:43,240
‎but it's disappointing
‎when she smells like cigarettes."

185
00:13:43,830 --> 00:13:48,170
‎The store manager said it was uncalled for
‎and that I shouldn't worry about it, but...

186
00:13:55,010 --> 00:13:58,600
‎But a complaint like that
‎makes me feel like a complete idiot.

187
00:14:04,980 --> 00:14:06,190
‎What a lonely person.

188
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:10,950
‎To lose faith in someone
‎you thought was great

189
00:14:11,020 --> 00:14:13,020
‎just because you see a new side to them, 

190
00:14:13,860 --> 00:14:15,650
‎even though they're still the same person...

191
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:21,740
‎But I'm overstepping here.

192
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:26,490
‎I don't even know which section
‎of the supermarket you work in--

193
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:34,510
‎Sorry. I didn't wear enough today, 
‎and now I can't stop sneezing--

194
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:42,850
‎Tayama! What are you--

195
00:14:47,730 --> 00:14:48,980
‎You can borrow this.

196
00:14:54,780 --> 00:14:56,370
‎It's warm.

197
00:14:56,440 --> 00:14:57,980
‎Thank you, Tayama.

198
00:15:12,170 --> 00:15:13,500
‎No. Thank you.

199
00:15:23,390 --> 00:15:26,390
‎And I'm sorry, Sasaki.

200
00:15:27,180 --> 00:15:29,810
‎-I can't drink coffee.
‎-What?

201
00:15:29,890 --> 00:15:32,310
‎You look surprised.

202
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:34,490
‎No, it's not that.

203
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:37,070
‎I actually can't have it either.

204
00:15:38,150 --> 00:15:40,570
‎Shall I just get a juice instead?

205
00:15:40,660 --> 00:15:43,290
‎I'll have a Depovita.

206
00:15:50,540 --> 00:15:52,710
‎What beautiful weather.

207
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:56,510
‎I love this spring weather.

208
00:15:57,300 --> 00:15:59,760
‎It seeps straight into my bones.

209
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:05,090
‎Especially after getting
‎absolutely chewed out by that client.

210
00:16:05,180 --> 00:16:07,720
‎I am so sorry! So very sorry!

211
00:16:08,350 --> 00:16:10,850
‎And now I have to go back to the office.

212
00:16:10,940 --> 00:16:13,820
‎I might get some food
‎from Super S on the way.

213
00:16:16,820 --> 00:16:19,740
‎Tayama must be on the night shift.

214
00:16:22,700 --> 00:16:24,830
‎I doubt she'll be there.

215
00:16:29,950 --> 00:16:31,580
‎Tayama--

216
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:36,090
‎Yamada?

217
00:16:36,590 --> 00:16:37,880
‎Hello.

218
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:40,380
‎What are you doing here?

219
00:16:40,460 --> 00:16:43,880
‎Don't tell me you work afternoons as well?

220
00:16:43,970 --> 00:16:46,850
‎It's okay, Sasaki. Calm down.

221
00:16:46,930 --> 00:16:49,140
‎I'm terribly sorry.

222
00:16:49,220 --> 00:16:51,470
‎I'm usually on the night shift, 

223
00:16:51,560 --> 00:16:54,230
‎but today I'm on the afternoon one
‎because we're so short-staffed.

224
00:16:54,310 --> 00:16:55,900
‎And as to why I'm here...

225
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:58,150
‎Calm down.

226
00:17:02,740 --> 00:17:05,079
‎This is the only vending machine we have.

227
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:07,369
‎I see.

228
00:17:07,450 --> 00:17:09,540
‎Are you off early today?

229
00:17:09,619 --> 00:17:13,040
‎No, I'm just heading back to work, 

230
00:17:13,119 --> 00:17:15,750
‎but I thought if Tayama were here, 
‎I might join her for a smoke--

231
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:18,290
‎I'm sorry, Yamada.

232
00:17:18,380 --> 00:17:20,670
‎I know I don't work here, but...

233
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:24,310
‎It's just that I was taking up
‎Tayama's kind invitation to join her.

234
00:17:24,380 --> 00:17:26,510
‎Please don't fault her for it.

235
00:17:27,760 --> 00:17:29,390
‎And so...

236
00:17:30,890 --> 00:17:33,140
‎It's fine, Sasaki.

237
00:17:33,230 --> 00:17:35,110
‎I already know.

238
00:17:35,900 --> 00:17:37,690
‎Tayama already told me.

239
00:17:37,770 --> 00:17:38,770
‎PON!

240
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:40,950
‎You really do talk
‎to her about everything.

241
00:17:41,030 --> 00:17:43,700
‎You must be really good friends.

242
00:17:46,280 --> 00:17:47,740
‎Dense-saki.

243
00:17:47,820 --> 00:17:48,820
‎DENSE-SAKI

244
00:17:48,910 --> 00:17:51,580
‎-Come again?
‎-Yes! We are great friends.

245
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:52,950
‎I thought as much.

246
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:56,210
‎I'm sure you have a lot in common.

247
00:17:56,290 --> 00:18:01,710
‎Seeing as you both have a real knack
‎when it comes to reading others.

248
00:18:04,800 --> 00:18:07,590
‎Oh, and Yamada...

249
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:08,680
‎Yes?

250
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:09,970
‎Well, 

251
00:18:10,890 --> 00:18:13,480
‎is Tayama doing okay?

252
00:18:14,850 --> 00:18:16,810
‎Yeah, she's fine.

253
00:18:18,190 --> 00:18:20,780
‎Are you referring
‎to the complaint she received?

254
00:18:20,860 --> 00:18:21,950
‎Yes.

255
00:18:22,020 --> 00:18:27,230
‎Sorry, but Tayama and I
‎were talking about it a little.

256
00:18:27,860 --> 00:18:29,990
‎I was wondering how she was doing.

257
00:18:32,030 --> 00:18:33,620
‎She's fine.

258
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:36,290
‎I was worried about her too, 

259
00:18:36,370 --> 00:18:40,290
‎but she said she had some ramen, 
‎went to bed, and forgot all about it.

260
00:18:42,130 --> 00:18:44,510
‎I see. Well, that's good to hear.

261
00:18:45,090 --> 00:18:50,050
‎I hope you'll continue
‎to lend her an ear, Sasaki.

262
00:18:50,140 --> 00:18:51,770
‎Yes, but...

263
00:18:52,350 --> 00:18:57,770
‎Is it really a good idea to rehash
‎something she's already put to bed?

264
00:18:58,730 --> 00:19:02,150
‎It doesn't have to be
‎about this thing in particular.

265
00:19:02,230 --> 00:19:06,570
‎I'll make sure to tell her
‎you were worried about her.

266
00:19:06,650 --> 00:19:07,650
‎COLD

267
00:19:08,650 --> 00:19:12,150
‎Are you sure?
‎I really wouldn't want to overstep.

268
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:14,830
‎You've already lent an ear.

269
00:19:14,910 --> 00:19:18,160
‎Would it really
‎still be considered overstepping?

270
00:19:19,710 --> 00:19:22,050
‎Well, I guess not.

271
00:19:23,960 --> 00:19:25,800
‎By the way, Yamada, 

272
00:19:26,380 --> 00:19:28,800
‎thank you for before.

273
00:19:30,050 --> 00:19:32,050
‎Tayama told me.

274
00:19:32,140 --> 00:19:36,980
‎She said you were worried about me
‎that time I was feeling down.

275
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:40,360
‎I didn't want to be a bother
‎by standing and chatting at your register, 

276
00:19:40,440 --> 00:19:43,110
‎so I never really
‎got the chance to thank you.

277
00:19:43,190 --> 00:19:44,440
‎It was nothing.

278
00:19:47,650 --> 00:19:51,070
‎I'd had a rough day at work, 
‎so I was really grateful.

279
00:19:51,700 --> 00:19:53,950
‎It meant a lot to know
‎that someone actually cared.

280
00:19:56,620 --> 00:19:57,660
‎It's fine.

281
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:01,950
‎But I hope I didn't overstep too much.

282
00:20:03,420 --> 00:20:05,760
‎You thought you were overstepping?

283
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:09,180
‎Look at that. Now I'm saying it.

284
00:20:11,300 --> 00:20:13,720
‎I guess that's just how it goes, huh?

285
00:20:17,510 --> 00:20:19,890
‎I'm sorry!
‎I'm prattling on and keeping you here.

286
00:20:19,980 --> 00:20:20,980
‎It's fine.

287
00:20:21,060 --> 00:20:26,480
‎I was happy I got to chat with you
‎the same way that Tayama does.

288
00:20:28,690 --> 00:20:30,530
‎Tayama may not be around, 

289
00:20:30,610 --> 00:20:33,150
‎but feel free to stay
‎and smoke if you'd like.

290
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:34,990
‎Thank you.

291
00:20:36,740 --> 00:20:40,120
‎Actually, I think I'll head back
‎without a smoke break today.

292
00:20:40,200 --> 00:20:42,740
‎I'd hate for you to end up
‎stuck with the smell.

293
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:46,750
‎Sorry to bother you on your break.

294
00:20:46,840 --> 00:20:47,930
‎See you.

295
00:20:53,840 --> 00:20:54,840
‎Sasaki.

296
00:20:54,930 --> 00:20:55,930
‎Yes?

297
00:21:08,520 --> 00:21:11,690
‎You had a flower petal
‎stuck to you this whole time.

298
00:21:13,360 --> 00:21:15,280
‎What? This whole time?

299
00:21:15,360 --> 00:21:16,360
‎You did.

300
00:21:16,450 --> 00:21:19,580
‎Fancy that. A flower petal
‎on some old geezer's head...

301
00:21:20,620 --> 00:21:23,670
‎You looked cute, so I didn't say anything.

302
00:21:23,750 --> 00:21:25,170
‎Sorry about that.

303
00:21:26,750 --> 00:21:29,880
‎No, thank you.

304
00:21:37,510 --> 00:21:39,550
‎Yamada can be a little...

305
00:21:40,850 --> 00:21:42,730
‎mischievous.

306
00:22:06,170 --> 00:22:08,460
‎Sasaki is so dense.

307
00:22:13,670 --> 00:22:14,960
‎It's weird.

308
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:39,890
‎Subtitle translation by: Rychelle Brittain
